                <pb facs="0176" n="110" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg110"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3731/510: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-02-06T17:00:00-05:00">February 6, 1934—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. Your despatch No. 394 of January 26. Your recommendations approved. In
                    accordance therewith please resume negotiations and press them as far as may be
                    possible to the most speedy conclusion. Keep Department currently informed of
                    progress.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
